## For Developers and AI Assistants

- [Instagram API](https://sssinstagram.com/api): REST access to publicly
  available Instagram media and profile data: usernames, profile bios and
  follower statistics, public posts and reels with captions and media URLs,
  timestamps, likes and comment counts, public stories and highlights,
  followers, following and post comments. The page describes the available
  data and how to request access.
- [Instagram MCP server](https://sssinstagram.com/mcp): Model Context Protocol
  server that gives AI assistants and agents access to public Instagram data —
  profile bios and follower statistics, public media URLs with captions and
  publication dates, stories and highlights, likes, comments and follower or
  following lists. It works with MCP-capable clients and agents such as
  ChatGPT, Codex, Claude, Cursor, Visual Studio Code and Gemini CLI. The page
  has the server address, setup steps for ChatGPT, Claude and any other MCP
  client, and the plans; 50 requests are free to try. Typical uses: influencer
  and creator research, profile and
  audience comparison, monitoring of posts, reels, stories and highlights, and
  engagement analysis.

